<title>USA: FSA qualifies six muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies six muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said on Thursday that it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Sara Scott Middle School District, Ind., $22.665 million.</p>
<p>--Lombard, Ill., $3.42 million installation contract certificates.</p>
<p>--Walled Lake Consolidated School District, Mich., $1.795 million consolidated bonds.</p>
<p>--Berlin Twp., N.J., $2.215 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Corinth CSD, N.Y., $3.935 million school district general obligations.</p>
<p>--Southern York County School District, Pa., $4.995 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
